---
layout: base.njk
title: "Explore your Clash Royale world with AI"
description: "Point Claude, ChatGPT or any AI agent at your own Clash Royale history and your clan's. Ask it anything, in plain language, over MCP."
permalink: /index.html
canonical: /
navActive: home
---
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px; align-items: flex-start; padding-top: 24px">
  <div style="flex: 1 1 480px; min-width: 0">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 14px">YOUR CLASH ROYALE WORLD · OPEN TO ANY AI AGENT · REMOTE MCP SERVER</div>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Point your AI at your Clash Royale world.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 14px">
      Clash Royale generates an enormous amount of detail about you and your
      clan — every battle, every deck, every promotion, every war. Elixir MCP
      opens all of it to <strong>Claude, ChatGPT, or whichever agent you
      already use</strong>, so you can explore it by just asking.
    </p>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 20px">
      <em>&ldquo;Which of my decks actually beats Hog cycle?&rdquo;</em>
      &nbsp;<em>&ldquo;Who in the clan is quietly carrying war?&rdquo;</em>
      &nbsp;<em>&ldquo;Am I better since I swapped to Firecracker?&rdquo;</em>
      Real questions, answered from the record — because we keep the history
      the game itself throws away.
    </p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap">
      <a class="btn btn--gold" href="#request">Request access</a>
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/docs/quickstart">Connect your agent →</a>
      <span style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim)">approval-gated · free while in early access</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="panel" style="flex: 1 1 320px; max-width: 420px">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <span style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted)">The corpus, live</span>
      <span class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 11px; color: var(--faint)">as of {{ t.newest_battle | day }}</span>
    </div>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr">
      <div style="padding: 16px; border-right: 1px solid var(--edge-soft); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge-soft)">
        <div class="stat__value" style="font-size: 30px">{{ t.battles | number }}</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); margin-top: 6px">battles recorded</div>
      </div>
      <div style="padding: 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge-soft)">
        <div class="stat__value" style="font-size: 30px">{{ t.players | number }}</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); margin-top: 6px">players observed</div>
      </div>
      <div style="padding: 16px; border-right: 1px solid var(--edge-soft)">
        <div class="stat__value" style="font-size: 30px">{{ t.clans | number }}</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); margin-top: 6px">clans observed</div>
      </div>
      <div style="padding: 16px">
        <div class="stat__value" style="font-size: 30px">{{ t.collectors_active | number }}</div>
        <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); margin-top: 6px">collectors active</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="padding: 10px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--edge-soft); display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim); flex-wrap: wrap">
      <span class="mono" style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px">oldest battle {{ t.oldest_battle | day }}</span>
      <span>·</span>
      <span>refreshed each deploy</span>
      <a style="margin-left: auto" href="/data/dashboard">Data ›</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 48px">
  <section class="panel" id="request">
    <div class="panel__head"><span class="panel-title">Request access</span></div>
    <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
      <div style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--faint)">
        Access is invite-approved while the recorder grows. Tell us who you are in the arena.
      </div>
      {#- The one interactive thing on the static half. Its script is
          /assets/request-form.js - an external file, not an inline
          block, because the CSP has no script-src 'unsafe-inline'
          (#25). Progressive enhancement is not available here (there
          is no non-JS POST target), so it fails loudly rather than
          silently swallowing a submission. -#}
      <form id="request-form" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
        <label>
          <span class="label">Email</span>
          <input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </label>
        <label>
          <span class="label">Your player tag</span>
          <input class="mono" name="player_tag" required placeholder="#20JJJ2CCRU" />
        </label>
        <label>
          <span class="label">Anything we should know? <span style="color: var(--dim)">(optional)</span></span>
          <input name="note" />
        </label>
        <p class="field-error" id="request-error" hidden></p>
        <div><button class="btn btn--gold" type="submit">Request access</button></div>
      </form>
      <div class="notice" id="request-sent" hidden>
        If your request is approved, you&rsquo;ll hear from us by email.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="panel__head"><span class="panel-title">How it works</span></div>
    <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      {%- set steps = [
        ["01", "Add your players and clans. Added means recorded — capture starts on the next poll and never stops."],
        ["02", "Connect your own AI agent over MCP. It sees your full recorded history with your entitlements applied."],
        ["03", "Ask it anything the game can't answer. Every number ships its sample size — observation, never opinion."]
      ] %}
      {%- for s in steps %}
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 12px">
        <span class="mono" style="color: var(--purple-link); font-weight: 600">{{ s[0] }}</span>
        <span style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55">{{ s[1] }}</span>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <span class="panel-title">What&rsquo;s new</span>
      <a class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; font-size: 11px" href="/updates">All updates ›</a>
    </div>
    <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      {%- for u in updates.slice(0, 4) %}
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 12px">
        <span class="mono" style="flex: 0 0 52px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--dim)">{{ u.date | replace("2026-", "") }}</span>
        <span style="font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.5">
          <strong>{{ u.title }}.</strong>
          <span style="color: var(--muted)">{{ u.body | clamp(140) }}</span>
        </span>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="panel" style="margin-top: 20px">
  <div class="panel__head"><span class="panel-title">Connect an agent</span></div>
  <div class="panel__body">
    <p style="color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 var(--s-3)">
      Point any MCP client at <code>{{ site.mcpUrl }}</code>. Your agent gets
      {{ tools.count }} tools across {{ tools.groups | length }} groups — the full
      reference is in <a href="/docs/tools">the docs</a>, and machine-readable at
      <a href="/tools.json">/tools.json</a> and <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="/assets/request-form.js" defer></script>
